		{
			"id": "e22Ik1tqkv0cotBJ6",
			"description": "Flak Jacket",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 7: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 7 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nSleeved version of the flak vest; partial arm coverage from the short armoured sleeves.\n\nLore: A sleeved variant of the vest, common where regiments expect close-quarters or urban combat and want some forearm protection against shrapnel and blades. Seen in Imperial Guard art and background across multiple Codex Astra Militarum editions.\n\nDesign: Torso DR 30 (flak anchor). Arms 23, a few points below torso per the framework's limb convention, keeping the 3:4 limb-to-torso ratio.",
			"tags": [
				"Body Armor",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
